#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa20dbfa-3f6f-5caf-9c10-906f2422f161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Trigonometric Equation Containing Tangent or Cotangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "859c250d-2b30-552d-ae3c-889d52560a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311332} {:answer/id #uuid "e51c143e-0228-535b-a244-e7bd8401d80b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311333} {:answer/id #uuid "9f536c92-6810-58a6-9a22-b4c02c0a7b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{7\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311334} {:answer/id #uuid "80a8e54a-5ed3-528c-8cf7-ee928714cd1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{4\\pi }{3}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311335} {:answer/id #uuid "ed428b22-42d0-5407-8593-3e4394c24e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed428b22-42d0-5407-8593-3e4394c24e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311336} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3331e7d-006c-5595-aeaf-5ee73606601c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "632e22b1-4c21-5851-8b21-7ad3340c1c1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-120782" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\sqrt{3}.$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{\\pi }{6}+n\\pi .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff04ceeb-c9f6-5562-b494-204eb62d7f5b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of the Points of Intersection of a Trigonometric Curve and a Horizontal Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c94e9d2b-284a-52d2-ba7f-baaff6fe66e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c94e9d2b-284a-52d2-ba7f-baaff6fe66e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311339} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0dc8136-78b1-51cd-8bb0-7981ddb1579d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d358064a-616d-5753-bcbb-bf73e5caf37c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d358064a-616d-5753-bcbb-bf73e5caf37c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311341} :answer-field/id #uuid "82d72786-5802-51bf-9552-45f2e9edc431" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a9d71686-b3e3-56dd-9035-b577ffa85e92" :question/math-academy-id "q-274743" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/c21ae590fc35738a016fd9c6191bd15685d0d0a6fb043f32aafaf8d01845d149.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a portion of the curve $y=2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and the line $y=2\\sqrt{3}.$\nFind an expression of the form\n$x=\\theta +n\\cdot b,$\nwhere $\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in radians, that generates the $x$-coordinates of the points of intersection.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of $\\pi .$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is \n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{3}+n\\cdot \\pi .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6a231e4f-d6b3-549f-81d4-30c0a883f9b4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Trigonometric Equation Containing Secant or Cosecant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93654fd7-0e54-51c9-837e-dd6985dd68d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 45^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, x = 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099299} {:answer/id #uuid "dfa9f6cc-b4f0-5d21-89fb-deaf3a4200ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 180^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099300} {:answer/id #uuid "e23b1a9f-8a14-5766-9dc5-638a195ffe90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 45^{∘} + n \\cdot 180^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099301} {:answer/id #uuid "e7956b6a-6245-5934-9a01-342c0e05d325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, x = 225^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099302} {:answer/id #uuid "f06a9b38-712d-531e-a657-16eefea410ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 45^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, x = 315^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93654fd7-0e54-51c9-837e-dd6985dd68d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 45^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}, x = 135^{∘} + n \\cdot 360^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099299} :answer-field/id #uuid "310eadae-dfda-5381-b749-e8f7af23d89a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9ba9ec8-f4a0-5e57-a91a-9ba206468825" :question/math-academy-id "q-30100" :question/problem "In degrees, what is the general solution to the equation $\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=2?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{csc}⁡x & =\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\text{arcsin}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{∘}\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the second quadrant, and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}={45}^{∘}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/978eaf470ef3b61ff7839471ed4ac46f320922b4d30f7f95566095124d0526d7.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$  lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & ={180}^{∘}-{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={45}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘},\\,x={135}^{∘}+n\\cdot {360}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa20dbfa-3f6f-5caf-9c10-906f2422f161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the General Solution to a Trigonometric Equation Containing Tangent or Cotangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3bb088b-fc9e-539b-b43d-ba82676fd51e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311344} {:answer/id #uuid "2cff173a-6d90-5010-8f96-79a850e718d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "157.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cff173a-6d90-5010-8f96-79a850e718d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "157.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311345} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5635edf-d997-5eb2-9b51-363cf90d8fa5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311343} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e093a81d-bfff-52b5-833b-b345c9c4f6ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e093a81d-bfff-52b5-833b-b345c9c4f6ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311347} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c344193-d1ed-5d28-8299-769f411a67b6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53ae4089-fae5-5e2e-bcd5-a0d30f0a1606" :question/math-academy-id "q-323844" :question/problem "Find the general solution to the equation $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1}$ in the form $x=\\theta +n\\cdot b$ where $\\theta \\in [0,{180}^{∘}),$ $n$ is an integer and $b$ is the period in degrees.\n\n*Hint: You may use the fact that $tan\\,({157.5}^{∘})=1-\\sqrt{2}.$*\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}${}^{∘}+\\,n\\,\\cdot $\n{{field-2}}${}^{∘}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x} & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}-1} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡x & =1-\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1-\\sqrt{2})={157.5}^{∘}\n$$\n\nThe tangent function has a period of ${180}^{∘}.$  Hence, the general solution for the given equation is\n\n$$\nx={157.5}^{∘}+n\\cdot {180}^{∘}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311348 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff04ceeb-c9f6-5562-b494-204eb62d7f5b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coordinates of the Points of Intersection of a Trigonometric Curve and a Horizontal Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4d68d7d-09fa-51cf-aa08-370f48525dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4d68d7d-09fa-51cf-aa08-370f48525dd2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311350} :answer-field/id #uuid "e7ba593a-f1f0-5418-a8eb-07e5de558f6b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd37bb4-91aa-515b-96a8-90ec14232643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bd37bb4-91aa-515b-96a8-90ec14232643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\pi}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311352} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1ed9ab0-0795-5822-bb80-8f5256a23ea0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b330735b-1d04-5ecb-8c1c-35b7ae8291f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b330735b-1d04-5ecb-8c1c-35b7ae8291f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311354} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce81aac1-d715-5cde-9352-1a11e1f69d4b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cedbaa79-cb49-5c7d-aff2-1b5dd0191c77" :question/math-academy-id "q-324057" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/435dd125850e3f97b5c3753a027f2db8718131ab499ef6711eaac637b1a022bd.png)\n\nThe graph shows a portion of the curve $y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the line $y=1.$ Find expressions of the form\n\n$$\nx={\\theta }_{1}+n\\cdot b,\\,x={\\theta }_{2}+n\\cdot b,\n$$\n\nwhere ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ ${\\theta }_{1},{\\theta }_{2}\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ $b$ is the period in radians, and $n$ is an integer, that generate the $x$-values of all of their points of intersection.\n\n${\\theta }_{1}=${{field-1}}$,\\,{\\theta }_{2}=$\n{{field-2}}$,\\,b=$\n{{field-3}}" :question/worked-solution "At the intersection points, the $y$-values are the same for both graphs. This gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=arcsin\\,(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\n$$\n\nOur first solution lies in the $1$st quadrant and has a reference angle of ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$ Since $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x>0,$ the second solution must lie in the $2$nd quadrant and it also has ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041314/assets/b0738a8a505b89ff687cb4de350a00f2e10d6209fbeee7dcdfdf0ee359a9cc3c.png)\n\nSince the second solution ${x}_{2}$ lies in the $2$nd quadrant, we can find it using the reference angle as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solutions are\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n,\\,x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}+2\\pi n.\n$$\n\nTherefore, since ${\\theta }_{1}<{\\theta }_{2},$ we have ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\text{ }{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6},\\text{ }\\text{and}\\text{ }b=2\\pi .$"}]}
